  "feel": "straight",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "notes": "Common time throughout. Each sung line occupies two bars; the verse is four lines (8 bars) and the chorus four lines (8 bars). The verse and the chorus deliberately move at different harmonic rates: the verse holds one chord per sung line (G, Em, C, G, two bars each) so the drop to the relative minor lands on the second line, while the chorus changes every bar (G G C G C G D G). The three-note anacrusis that opens each verse line sits at the end of the preceding phrase, and the very first one lives in the last beat and a half of the intro.",
